# Language and Comments (facturador-crecer-api)

## Language

- Write all code in English: identifiers, file names, types, comments, logs for developers, commit-oriented messages in code.
- Allowed Spanish (or business locale) only for:
  - Values persisted in the database when the domain already stores Spanish
  - Error messages returned to the client / end user
  - Existing domain labels that must match stored data (status codes, catalog values, etc.)
- Do not mix Spanish variable or function names with English ones.

```typescript
// GOOD
throw new Error('El recibo no existe'); // client-facing
logger.error('Failed to create receipt', { receiptId }); // developer-facing

// BAD
const reciboId = receipt.id;
```

## Comments

- Every exported function, use case method, controller handler, domain service method, and repository method must have a short one-line comment describing its purpose.
- Keep comments brief (one line; two only if necessary). No essays.
- Do not comment obvious lines (`// increment counter`, `// return result`).
- Comment business rules, constraints, and non-obvious decisions when needed.

```typescript
/** Creates a receipt and persists it through the repository. */
async run(receiptData: ReceiptData): Promise<Receipt> {
```
